## Project-Specific SOP Considerations
- meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel between runner and coders — no stdout parsing
- No pre-invocation sidecar writes or markdown write-backs
- Explicit exception routing with failure classification (AUTO_RETRYABLE, HUMAN_RETRY_REQUIRED, FATAL)
- Model alias resolution via model_mapping.json (e.g., deepseek-chat → qwen coder with DeepSeek API)
- Multi-coder support (Claude, Codex, Qwen) with per-step coder selection
- Human-in-the-loop approval gates at review steps
- Refine/replan loops with bounded iterations (max 2 refine, max 1 replan)
- Cross-project scaffolding support via --target-project-root flag
- Deterministic validation step (validate_delivery_docs) — not a coder invocation
- No external dependencies beyond coder CLIs — minimal Python dependency footprint
- UKBE spec compliance: contract-driven artifact generation, budget enforcement, reproducibility via snapshots

